Subject: [PATCH 02/12] Document pure Bend2 build admission and bootstrap
 boundary

Record the canonical shared cgroup slice, aggregate capacity decision,
RLIMIT_AS and process-tree enforcement, compiler runner entry, direct
check-only coverage, cancellation, receipts, workflow guard and the exact
bootstrap dependency for #677/#819.
---
 docs/bend2/build-admission.md | 161 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 161 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 docs/bend2/build-admission.md

diff --git a/docs/bend2/build-admission.md b/docs/bend2/build-admission.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..622b6042
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bend2/build-admission.md
@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@
+# Native build admission
+
+Status: design for #677 and #819. The current branch carries a workflow guard.
+The Bend2 source changes below are not compiled in this branch. The host slice and
+the runner bootstrap are prerequisites owned by root.
+
+## Scope
+
+One admission decision covers every native compiler execution: the coordinator
+Main generation, focused test builds, packaging, fixture compilers and direct
+`bend --check-only` calls. The decision uses actual host capacity and actual
+aggregate memory use. A repeated request for the same source, toolchain, entry
+and output returns the retained execution or its receipt.
+
+## Canonical host admission
+
+The canonical admission object is a systemd cgroup v2 slice at
+`/sys/fs/cgroup/baton2-build.slice`. Root creates it with a real `MemoryMax`
+budget and `Delegate=yes`, and grants both runner accounts write access to the
+delegated subtree. The path is host-wide: it does not depend on a clone, a
+worktree, a user ID, `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, a temporary directory or a mount
+namespace. `/sys/fs/cgroup` is mounted in both runner services today; the
+runner must refuse with `slice-unavailable` when it is not.
+
+Each admitted execution creates a unique sub-cgroup under the slice, writes its
+`memory.max` budget, moves the runner into it, and then starts the compiler.
+Compiler children inherit the sub-cgroup, so the whole process tree is bounded
+by the same allocation. The slice's `memory.max` bounds the sum of all
+sub-cgroups.
+
+There is no per-user fallback and no guessed global floor. When the slice is
+missing or unlimited, admission refuses and reports the exact paths and values
+it read. Root owns the slice budget.
+
+## Decision inputs
+
+- `memory.max` and `memory.current` of the slice: actual aggregate capacity and
+  actual aggregate use.
+- A demand in KiB from the exact build manifest for full generation. The
+  manifest records measured peak RSS for the same source commit, compiler
+  digest, entry and output. A manifest that does not match refuses with
+  `manifest-mismatch`; a missing manifest refuses with `manifest-absent`.
+- A declared focused budget from the workflow or caller for a focused build.
+- A retained-C manifest for the `reuse` class. A matching retained-C manifest
+  admits the copy and link step with a small focused budget; it does not require
+  full-generation capacity.
+
+Admission admits when `memory.current + demand <= memory.max`. Focused builds
+may run concurrently while the sum of their budgets and current use stays within
+the slice. Full generation and focused builds use the same aggregate rule; the
+class changes the demand source, not the lock order.
+
+## Resource enforcement
+
+Before the compiler starts, the host boundary sets `RLIMIT_AS` to the admitted
+budget for the runner and its descendants. `RLIMIT_AS` needs no privilege and
+is inherited across `exec`. The sub-cgroup `memory.max` enforces the aggregate
+process-tree budget against actual allocation. `memory.peak`, `memory.swap.max`
+and `memory.events` are read into the receipt.
+
+The runner writes its own PID into the sub-cgroup `cgroup.procs` before it
+spawns the compiler. No compiler or compiler child starts outside the
+sub-cgroup.
+
+## Compiler entry and runner contract
+
+The `bend` entry used by builds is a runner, not the raw compiler binary. The
+runner command is:
+
+```
+baton2 build-admission --entry ENTRY --output OUTPUT --class CLASS \
+  --demand-kib N --receipt PATH --real-bend REAL_BEND -- ARGS...
+```
+
+All arguments pass through, including `--check-only`, `-o`, `--version` and
+direct fixture invocations. The toolchain installation places this runner at
+the `bend` path used by `BEND`, `.bend/bin/bend` and the workflow toolchain
+directory. The build script, `prepare-native-compiler.py`, `package-native.py`,
+`accept-native-receive.py`, `trial-start.sh` and direct test invocations use
+that entry. A raw compiler path remains available only to the bootstrap step.
+
+## Bootstrap dependency
+
+The runner is a product command in the Baton binary. The bootstrap is the single
+compiler invocation that builds a Baton binary containing the admission command
+from a source tree that does not yet have it. The bootstrap rule:
+
+1. Use the installed Baton release binary whose `build-admission` action is
+   present, with its recorded executable digest and version.
+2. Run that bootstrap build with `RLIMIT_AS` set to 8 GiB for the build process
+   tree and, when available, inside the shared slice.
+3. Record the source commit, compiler digest, command, limits and exit status in
+   the bootstrap receipt.
+
+When no released Baton binary contains the command, root supplies an approved
+runner binary and its digest. The bootstrap is the only compiler path outside
+the runner. Every later build, including `--check-only`, uses the runner.
+
+## Cancellation
+
+The sub-cgroup path is written into the receipt before the compiler starts.
+On SIGINT, SIGTERM or SIGHUP the runner writes `1` to the sub-cgroup
+`cgroup.kill`, records the signal, and leaves the receipt in place. The workflow
+job timeout and step cancellation therefore terminate the whole compiler tree,
+not only the step shell. A runner lost by SIGKILL leaves the sub-cgroup and the
+start receipt; the next admission reads `memory.current` and `cgroup.procs` and
+reports the retained execution.
+
+## Receipts
+
+Each attempt writes one JSON receipt before execution and updates it after exit.
+Fields: schema, class, decision, cause, source commit and status, compiler path
+and digest, entry, output, command, slice path, sub-cgroup path, `memory.max`,
+`memory.current`, `memory.peak`, `memory.swap.max`, `memory.events`,
+`RLIMIT_AS`, pid, pgid, start and end times, exit status or forwarded signal,
+and retained-C manifest identity for the reuse class.
+
+## Workflow changes
+
+- Push-triggered automatic validation is removed until the runner and slice are
+  installed. The current branch removes it and adds an exact `source_commit`
+  dispatch input.
+- The dispatch path checks out `source_commit`, records it, and asserts the
+  checkout equals it.
+- A preflight job on the homelab runner reads the slice capacity before the
+  candidate, target and Darwin jobs. The build jobs depend on it.
+- Candidate and target builds use the same runner entry. A completed target
+  build run is reused only when its manifest matches the target commit and
+  toolchain.
+- The Darwin job uses the same runner contract; macOS capacity must come from
+  its own cgroup or an approved remote placement. It does not fall back to an
+  unlimited local build.
+- Dispatch authorization is restricted to trusted actors; the pull-request
+  ref limit and the supported dispatch route are documented in
+  `docs/bend2/native-artifacts.md`.
+
+## Source changes for review
+
+- `bend2/src/coordinator/build-admission.bend`: decision types, aggregate
+  capacity rule, manifest matching, receipt schema and the runner action.
+- `bend2/src/coordinator/commands.bend` and `main.bend`: the
+  `build-admission` command and its argument parsing.
+- `bend2/src/host/build-admission.bend` and `bend2/src/host/build-admission.c`:
+  cgroup read/write, sub-cgroup creation and removal, self PID, `setrlimit`,
+  process-group spawn, wait and signal forwarding. This is the narrow platform
+  boundary.
+- `bend2/scripts/build-native.sh`: call the runner instead of the raw compiler;
+  keep the bootstrap branch behind the recorded release digest.
+- `bend2/scripts/prepare-native-compiler.py` and the workflow compiler setup:
+  install the runner at the `bend` entry and retain the raw compiler path for
+  the bootstrap only.
+- `bend2/test/build-admission.py` is removed. Tests become Bend2 law fixtures
+  plus a focused shell fixture that exercises the runner with a stub compiler.
+
+## Prerequisites owned by root
+
+- Create and delegate `/sys/fs/cgroup/baton2-build.slice` with an actual
+  `MemoryMax` and access for both runner users.
+- Install a Baton release binary containing `build-admission`, or provide the
+  approved bootstrap runner and digest.
+- Confirm `/sys/fs/cgroup` is visible in both runner mount namespaces.
-- 
2.43.0


